auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # TripMate API

  Bearer auth is applied at the collection level (uses the `{{token}}` env var).
  Public endpoints (register, login, trip preview) override this with `auth: none`.

  ## Quick start
  1. Select the **Local** environment (top-right).
  2. Run **Auth > Register** (or **Login**) — this auto-saves `token` and `userId`.
  3. Run **Trips > Create Trip** — auto-saves `tripId` and `inviteToken`.
  4. Run **Expenses > Create Expense** — auto-saves `expenseId`.
  5. Everything else reads those env vars automatically.
}
